# Wave W17-X (Route 210 — North): waybell — a fog waybell at the road’s mouth: two posts and a crossbar carrying one small brass bell, rung by the wind off the mountain so walkers navigate by ear (design: waybells standing in the murk; in fog, walk by ear: the grass keeps talking). On fog turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from the fleet’s single posts by the frame entire: a post marks a place, a waybell marks a way through weather.
